1. Definitions

"Covered Materials" means the original source code, object code, documentation,
visual and interaction design, artwork, illustrations, graphics, animations,
layout, text, and other materials in this project that are owned or controlled
by the Batify project rightsholder(s), including modified and compiled versions
of those materials.

"Design" means the distinctive visual, interaction, and presentation choices
embodied in Batify, including its page composition and layouts; envelope and
gift-opening presentation; illustrations, icons, and decorative artwork;
typography and type treatments; color combinations; shapes, motion, and
transitions; and the selection, arrangement, and coordination of those elements.
This definition covers the protectable expression and overall presentation of
the project, not general ideas, methods, functionality, or industry conventions
that are not protectable under applicable law.

"Rightsholder" means the person or entity that owns or is authorized to license
the applicable Covered Materials.

"Third-Party Materials" means software, fonts, services, artwork, or other
materials in or used by this project that are owned by someone other than a
Rightsholder.

"User Content" means content submitted to or created by an end user of the
hosted Batify service, including birthday letters, names, wishes, photographs,
videos, and payment evidence.

